Law texts

The texts in this repository are Ordinances of the State of Sarawak as published, in English, on Sarawak LawNet
(https://lawnet.sarawak.gov.my) by the State Attorney-General's Chambers, Sarawak: the online versions of the updated
text of the reprints, each incorporating all amendments up to the date its cover states.

- Copyright: the Copyright Act 1987 [Act 332] of Malaysia, section 3, defines "literary work" and ends: "but does not
  include official texts of the Government or statutory bodies of a legislative or regulatory nature, or judicial
  decisions, or political speeches and political debates, or speeches delivered in the course of legal proceedings,
  and the official translation thereof". (Quoted from the Attorney General's Chambers' online reprint of Act 332, as
  at 1 July 2012.) The Ordinances are official texts of a legislative nature.
- The site's footer reads "Copyright 2011 Sarawak Government. All Rights Reserved." Its disclaimer gives no warranty
  of completeness or accuracy and says: "A print out from this System is not a copy of the State Government Gazette
  printed by the State Government Printer. For the purpose of any legal proceeding, authoritative copy of the law as
  printed by the State Government Printer should be used." The site states no terms that restrict reuse.
- The texts are reproduced without change to their wording; only the arrangement (one file per section, one paragraph
  per line) is Lexifina's. The State Attorney-General's Chambers does not endorse this repository.

Attribution: Source: State Attorney-General's Chambers, Sarawak, Sarawak LawNet, https://lawnet.sarawak.gov.my.

